    "description": "## Summary\n\nWhen an Active Player has no completed sign-ups (or other qualifying activity) in the last 90 days, set their Status to Inactive.\n\n## Context\n\nWithout an aging rule, players stay Active forever and reporting overstates the active base. The client set the threshold at **90 days without qualifying activity**. Qualifying activity is measured by Account.Last_Activity_Date__c.\n\n## Current state\n\nNo scheduled automation exists on Account. Player_Status_Reason\\__c already includes the value Inactivity. Field history tracking on Player_Statusc is off. In Partial today no Player is Active and no Last_Activity_Date_\\_c is set, so first activation is safe by definition.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. NEW schedule-triggered flow Player_Scheduled_Set_Inactive, daily 02:00 ET, on Account. Selects Players (Player record type) that are **Active** with a Last Activity Date **more than 90 days in the past**. Players at Pending, Banned, or Inactive, or with a blank Last Activity Date, are never touched. How eligibility is filtered (entry criteria vs. in-flow decision) is the developer's call — the boundary behavior is defined in the acceptance criteria.\n2. Per eligible record: set Inactive and Player_Status_Reason__c = Inactivity. (Audit stamping via BUILD-251; the stamped updater will read \"Automated Process\" — expected.)\n3. The 90-day threshold must be defined in **exactly one place** in the flow, named and documented so it's easy to find and change. Upgrade to a custom setting only if the client asks to tune it.\n4. Enable field history tracking on Player_Status__c (audit trail for all status changes).\n\nTesting note: feel free to adjust the inactivity threshold to 2–3 days or shorter to confirm the scheduled flow runs as expected, or manually set the Completed Dates/Activity Dates to simulate older completions.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. An Active Player 91+ days stale flips to Inactive with Reason = Inactivity on the next run; exactly 90 days stays Active (boundary).\n2. Must NOT evaluate: blank Last_Activity_Date__c, Pending, Banned, or players reactivated since their last activity.\n3. A reactivated player is only re-flipped after a fresh 90-day lapse.\n4. Bulk-safe at 200+ eligible records.\n\n## Output\n\nScheduled flow deployed + activated in Partial SB; history tracking enabled; API names + first-run record count recorded on this ticket; requirements doc updated.",
